        "problem": "Express ${cos}^{2}\u2061{14}^{\u2218}-{sin}^{2}\u2061{14}^{\u2218}$ as a single trigonometric ratio.",
        "worked_solution": "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n{cos}^{2}\u2061x-{sin}^{2}\u2061x=\\operatorname{cos}\u20612x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x={14}^{\u2218}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{cos}^{2}\u2061{14}^{\u2218}-{sin}^{2}\u2061{14}^{\u2218} & =\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(2\\cdot {14}^{\u2218}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}\u2061{28}^{\u2218}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
